{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Concerning my judgment</b> — because I seek justice, they say that I lie." "<b>I am pierced</b> — its meaning is 'I am struck,' like the expression אָנוּשָׁה מַכָּתֵךְ (your wound is incurable)." "<b>Without transgression</b> — without guilt. Or it means 'I am pierced,' even though I have not transgressed, like the expression אֶל־הַשַּׂעַרָה וְלֹא יַחֲטִיא (to the target, and it does not miss); and it is by way of analogy."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {2 "The phrase אנוש חצי is difficult: Ibn Ezra may be reading a form of אנש (to be diseased/incurable) in the verse, or the text may be corrupt; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:26.728056414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}